<CompareLayout
	slug="open-source-saas-starters"
	h1="Rocketflare vs BoxyHQ, Open SaaS, Epic Stack and other open-source starters"
	lede="The free starters are good teachers. Most show you the shape of an app, wire in sign-in and maybe Stripe, and leave organisations, jobs, an admin area and AI to you. Several have also gone quiet. Rocketflare is free under the same MIT terms, and is the whole multi-tenant application, actively released."
	glance={[
		{ label: 'They give you', body: 'A skeleton or a single-user app, sometimes with payments.' },
		{ label: 'Rocketflare gives you', body: 'A complete multi-tenant app with SSO, jobs, dashboards, an admin area and an AI layer, all tested.' },
		{ label: 'Also free', body: 'MIT, like most of them. The difference is how much is already there, and whether it is still maintained.' },
	]}
	shortAnswer="If you want a small reference to learn from, or a single-user app with payments, use Epic Stack, the Next.js SaaS Starter or Open SaaS. If you are building a B2B product in TypeScript with AI at its core, Rocketflare is the most complete free starting point we know of: organisations, roles, SSO, jobs, dashboards, durable agents and a knowledge base, MIT licensed and actively released."
